What is that an arraylist has been passed in , which may or may not have a size bigger that the actual number of elements that are meant to be flushed to the circular buffer . thus the ' uptoindex ' parameter specifies the number of elements that need to be flushed starting from index 0 . note that after flushing , the circular buffer may return a memory unit ( of type t ) for reuse in the list , if the circular buffer popped off memory to preserve its circular nature . or it may just return null if nothing was popped off . either way , the list that is returned by this method , is of the same size as the list passed in , as arraylists can hold null elements . the only difference is that the list returned will have elements that reference old popped - off memory from the circular - buffer or null ?
